% Test cases for the tracheostomy care supplies policy
% (tracheostomy_supplies.le): synthetic claims, one or two per criterion of
% LCD L33832 and per payment condition of dmepos.le and Policy Article
% A52492. Findings are recorded as the treating practitioner's or the
% Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the answer conditional. Supplies
% are a one-off or a refill: no rental month. The queries: whether the
% claim is payable (the first query, so "stage" reads its checklist),
% whether it is reasonable and necessary, and what minimal change would make
% it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base tracheostomy_supplies cases includes these resources:
    tracheostomy_supplies.

the knowledge base tracheostomy_supplies cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for a month of care kits (A4629, 31 a month) for an
% established tracheostomy: the tracheostomy of October 2025, expected to
% remain open, the tracheostomy status code on the claim, and every
% documentation requirement in the record. The prosthetic benefit asks
% nothing about the residence. No code of the policy is on the CMS
% face-to-face list: the order need only reach the supplier before the date
% of service.
scenario care_kits_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the care kits.
    the HCPCS code of the care kits is "A4629".
    the care kits is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 31.
    Ann had an open surgical tracheostomy on 2025-10-01.
    the tracheostomy of Ann is expected to be open for at least three months.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "Z93.0".
    the order for the care kits is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the care kits is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the care kits includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the care kits includes order date.
    the order for the care kits includes description of the item.
    the order for the care kits includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the care kits includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the care kits was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the care kits was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the care kits.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The starter kit (A4625): ten days after the tracheostomy it is covered;
% twenty days after, no longer.
scenario starter_kit_timing is:
    claim 1 is for the starter kit.
    the HCPCS code of the starter kit is "A4625".
    the starter kit is furnished to Ben.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-02-11.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 10.
    claim 2 is for the late starter kit.
    the HCPCS code of the late starter kit is "A4625".
    the late starter kit is furnished to Ben.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-02-21.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 10.
    Ben had an open surgical tracheostomy on 2026-02-01.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The usual quantities: one tube (A7520, 1 per 3 months) for a three-month
% supply is within the maximum, two are not; 124 dressings (A4623, 62 a
% month) for two months are within it, 130 are not.
scenario usual_quantities is:
    claim 1 is for the tube.
    the HCPCS code of the tube is "A7520".
    the tube is furnished to Cy.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 1.
    claim 2 is for the tubes.
    the HCPCS code of the tubes is "A7520".
    the tubes is furnished to Cy.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 2.
    claim 3 is for the dressings.
    the HCPCS code of the dressings is "A4623".
    the dressings is furnished to Cy.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 2 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 3 is 124.
    claim 4 is for the extra dressings.
    the HCPCS code of the extra dressings is "A4623".
    the extra dressings is furnished to Cy.
    claim 4 is for a supply of 2 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 4 is 130.
    Cy had an open surgical tracheostomy on 2025-06-15.
    the finding excess quantity of supplies explained about Cy is unsupported, according to the reviewer, because "the record gives no reason for more than the listed amounts".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 3 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A greater quantity than the usual maximum (45 care kits in a month):
% covered on the treating practitioner's explanation in Dee's record; not
% covered where the Council finds Eve's record explains nothing.
scenario excess_quantity_explained is:
    claim 1 is for the care kits.
    the HCPCS code of the care kits is "A4629".
    the care kits is furnished to Dee.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 45.
    Dee had an open surgical tracheostomy on 2025-06-15.
    the finding excess quantity of supplies explained about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "copious purulent secretions since the stoma infection of January require the dressing and ties to be changed three times a day".
    claim 2 is for the second care kits.
    the HCPCS code of the second care kits is "A4629".
    the second care kits is furnished to Eve.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 45.
    Eve had an open surgical tracheostomy on 2025-06-15.
    the finding excess quantity of supplies explained about Eve is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the only explanation in the file is the supplier's statement that the beneficiary asked for more kits; the physician's notes do not mention the frequency of care".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A plug (A7527, 2 per 3 months) furnished to Fay is covered; the tube
% (A7520) claimed beside it is not; a tracheostomy mask (A7523) is never
% covered.
scenario plug_tube_and_mask is:
    claim 1 is for the plug.
    the HCPCS code of the plug is "A7527".
    the plug is furnished to Fay.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 2.
    claim 2 is for the tube.
    the HCPCS code of the tube is "A7520".
    the tube is furnished to Fay.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 1.
    claim 3 is for the mask.
    the HCPCS code of the mask is "A7523".
    the mask is furnished to Fay.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 3 is 1.
    Fay had an open surgical tracheostomy on 2025-06-15.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Reasonable and necessary with its order and delivery, but the record does
% not say the tracheostomy is expected to remain open for three months
% (Policy Article A52492): payable fails at the remedy, and the flip adds
% that statement.
scenario no_three_month_expectation is:
    claim 1 is for the care kits.
    the HCPCS code of the care kits is "A4629".
    the care kits is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 31.
    Ann had an open surgical tracheostomy on 2025-10-01.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "Z93.0".
    the order for the care kits is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the care kits is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the care kits includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the care kits includes order date.
    the order for the care kits includes description of the item.
    the order for the care kits includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the care kits includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the care kits was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the care kits was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the care kits.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the tracheostomy of Ann is expected to be open for at least three months"]].

% The dispensing cap: for Gus, in a nursing facility, a one-month supply of
% collars (A7526) is payable and a three-month supply is not.
scenario nursing_facility_dispensing is:
    claim 1 is for the collars.
    the HCPCS code of the collars is "A7526".
    the collars is furnished to Gus.
    the residence of Gus is nursing facility.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 31.
    claim 2 is for the quarterly collars.
    the HCPCS code of the quarterly collars is "A7526".
    the quarterly collars is furnished to Gus.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 93.
    Gus had an open surgical tracheostomy on 2025-10-01.
    the tracheostomy of Gus is expected to be open for at least three months.
    the diagnosis code of Gus is "Z93.0".
    the order for the collars is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the collars is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the collars includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the collars includes order date.
    the order for the collars includes description of the item.
    the order for the collars includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the collars includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the collars was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the collars was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the collars.
    the order for the quarterly collars is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the quarterly collars is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the quarterly collars includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the quarterly collars includes order date.
    the order for the quarterly collars includes description of the item.
    the order for the quarterly collars includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the quarterly collars includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the quarterly collars was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the quarterly collars was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the quarterly collars.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% A refill of care kits, the supply running out on 1 June, the beneficiary
% contacted on 15 May and the kits delivered on 25 May: within the refill
% windows of dmepos.le, with continued need and use in the record.
scenario refill is:
    claim 1 is for the care kits.
    the HCPCS code of the care kits is "A4629".
    the care kits is furnished to Ann.
    claim 1 is a refill.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-05-25.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 31.
    the current supply of the care kits is expected to end on 2026-06-01.
    the beneficiary affirmed the need for the refill of the care kits on 2026-05-15.
    the medical record documents continued need for the care kits on 2026-04-10.
    the record documents continued use of the care kits on 2026-04-10.
    Ann had an open surgical tracheostomy on 2025-10-01.
    the tracheostomy of Ann is expected to be open for at least three months.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "Z93.0".
    the order for the care kits is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the care kits is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the care kits includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the care kits includes order date.
    the order for the care kits includes description of the item.
    the order for the care kits includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the care kits includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the care kits was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the care kits was delivered on 2026-05-25.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the care kits.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].
